# This repo is developed on Windows and deployed on Linux. Without this, a
# working tree checked out on Windows can commit CRLF, and a CRLF shell script
# or config fails on Ubuntu in ways that are painful to diagnose ("bad
# interpreter: /bin/bash^M").
#
# Normalise everything text to LF in the repository. Git still gives Windows
# users CRLF in their working tree when core.autocrlf says so; what changes is
# what gets stored and therefore what Linux checks out.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that MUST be LF wherever they land: they are read by Linux tooling
# inside containers, or by a shell.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.cfg       text eol=lf
*.xml       text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf

# Windows-only helpers: CRLF is correct for these, and PowerShell is happier.
*.ps1       text eol=crlf

# Never touched.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.db        binary
*.pickle    binary
*.quar      binary
